    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Bennetts Auctioneers are delighted to present No. 2  Wilfield Park to the market. This is an excellent opportunity to acquire this superb property located in this much sought after and convenient location. Features of the property include gas fired central heating, private off street parking for two cars,  beautiful bay windows, attractive spacious rear garden and excellent potential to enhance and extend subject to p.p. Extending to approximately 153.8 sq. m the accommodation briefly comprises a entrance hall, hallway, kitchen/dining room, sun room, living room, study, utility and shower room completing the ground floor accommodation. The first floor comprises three spacious bedrooms and a family bathroom.\r\nExternally, to the front, the property is approached by a gravelled driveway providing generous off street parking. Mature hedging and established planting provide excellent privacy, while the attractive bay fronted façade adds to the property’s distinctive character. A pathway to the side provides convenient access to the rear garden.\r\n\r\nTo the rear, the property enjoys a beautifully maintained and exceptionally private garden, predominantly laid in lawn and framed by an abundance of mature trees, hedging and established shrubbery. A charming pathway leads through the garden to a secluded seating area, creating an ideal setting for outdoor dining and entertaining. The Sun room  enjoys a wonderful outlook over the garden and further enhances the connection between the house and its outdoor space.\r\n\r\nThis charming, detached family home presents a rare opportunity to acquire a property of considerable character on one of Sandymount’s most desirable roads, combining generous accommodation, wonderful privacy and superb potential to further enhance and extend, subject to the necessary planning permission"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Hall: 1.74m x 2.60m tiled flooring \r\n\r\nHallway 1.15m x 4.47m tiled flooring \r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Room: 3.35m x 7.66m tiled flooring, abundance of natural light, feature solid fuel stove, recessed lighting, contemporary fitted kitchen,  granite worktops, stainless steel sink, range of eye to floor level units, featuring  induction hob and extractor fan \r\n\r\nSun Room: 4.27m x 3.51m tiled flooring, Velux skylight, excellent natural light with extensive glazing, attractive views over the mature, landscaped garden, french doors opening directly onto the garden \r\n\r\nLiving Room: 3.41m x 5.01m wood flooring, coving, marble fireplace, striking bay window to the front providing excellent natural light\r\n \r\nStudy: 4.40m x 3.52m wood flooring,  recessed lighting, large window to the front \r\n\r\nShower Room: 2.12m x 1.76m floor to ceiling tiling, shower unit, w.h.b, w.c\r\n\r\nUtility Room: 3.12m x 2.42m tiled flooring, feature velux skylight ample storage space, plumbed for washer/dryer, door to rear garden \r\n\r\nFirst Floor \r\nBedroom 1: 3.40m x 5.01m wood flooring, two integrated wardrobes, recessed lighting, feature bay window to the front \r\n\r\nBedroom 2: 4.26m x 3.26m wood flooring, integrated wardrobe,  recessed lighting, window to rear \r\n\r\nBedroom 3 3.51m x 2.58m wood flooring, window to the rear, recessed lighting \r\n\r\nBathroom: 3.26m x 1.60m floor to ceiling tiling, bath/shower unit, w.h.b, w.c \r\n\r\nTotal Floor Area: c. 153.8 sq. m.\r\n\r\nAsking Price: €1,745,000\r\n\r\nBER: D\r\n\r\nBER No.:  119697134\r\n\r\nEnergy Performance Indicator: 39,486 kWh/m2/yr\r\n\r\nSale Negotiator: Allie Parker"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Beautifully presented three bedroom detached family residence in a highly desirable setting\r\n\r\nSuperb potential to further enhance and extend the existing accommodation, subject to the necessary planning permission.\r\n\r\nPrivate off street parking for two cars and convenient side access to the property\r\n\r\nBeautifully maintained and exceptionally private rear garden, featuring a charming pathway framed by mature trees and established shrubbery\r\n\r\nCharming bay windows enhance both the living room and master bedroom\r\n\r\nSuperbly positioned on one of Sandymount's most sought-after roads, just moments from the village and its excellent range of amenities.\r\n\r\nTotal floor area of c. 153.8 sq. m."
      },
      {
